-- The interleaved wand (w3-b): [DP, Triple, SB, DP, SB, SB] — the general binding, first spelling: gamma over an order-derived srel. Twin of w3-modifier-chain.bqn (the interleaved section).
-- binds' is geometry from the slot ground: fiber of each projectile = the modifiers whose next-projectile-at-or-after is that slot (the .bqn's NextP, inverted), derived the way moore derives from the lattice and listed the same way. The damage write is then the ex36 grouped fold — DP0 rides through the Triple onto its first bolt, DP3 onto the next, and the shortcut's answer (both on the block's first projectile) is provably wrong here.
--! registry w3-modifier-chain-b
--! expect bal = 0 1 3 2 2 1 0
--! expect minBal = 0 1 1 1 1 1 0
--! expect member = 0 1 1 1 1 1 1
--! expect damage = 0 0 0 13 0 13 3

Spell , Bal = 1 + (+\ (DrawAdd - 1) @ Spell)
Spell , MinBal = 0 - (max\ (0 - Bal) @ Spell)
Spell @ deck & (Slot == 0 | prev.MinBal > 0) , +Member
Spell & Proj & Member , Damage += 10 * (#/ (binds' & (Mod & Member)))
